{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Come on through. The N11 was a nightmare, I was twenty minutes getting past Bray in that rain.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Tell me about it. We crawled from Greystones, rain coming sideways the whole way.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Left at half seven and your one in front had the hazards on, not a bother on her. I was fit to be tied.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): And the radio full of the hurling. Kilkenny again. I couldn't be listening.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): My grandson was texting the scores from the couch. Eight years of age and he thinks he's the manager. An opinion on every puck-out.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (NURSE): Ha. Grand. Chart's on the desk. Doctor's just outside.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (DOCTOR): Morning. What brought you?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): A lump. I found it in the shower, left breast. I'm 46 and I can't get it out of my head.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, about 3 weeks. I kept hoping it would just go.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sore?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not painful at all. That's what has me terrified, I read painless is worse.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any discharge from the nipple?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never. I checked.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (DOCTOR): Lumps anywhere else? Under the arm?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either. I had a feel and there's nothing else.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (DOCTOR): Redness? Skin pulling in?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Same as the other side, far as I can see.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fever? Weight going down?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Sorry, does the no pain make it more likely to be cancer? I haven't slept right since.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Pain tells me nothing. Right. You have asthma on the file, yes?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, since I was about sixteen. Still have it.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Wheezy at the minute? Chest tight?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. At night, if I'm after the stairs.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (DOCTOR): Preventer inhaler?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): I was on the brown one, err, clennil I think, but I stopped it myself. Just the blue ventolin now.",
  "[SEG0028] person_4 (DOCTOR): Clenil, yes. How much Ventolin?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Two puffs, maybe 3 times a week? I'm not great at remembering whether I've taken it. Should I start the brown one again, is two puffs even enough?",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): Leave the Clenil off. Two puffs is the usual amount. Not today's problem. Your mother had breast cancer?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): At fifty five. She's ten years clear now, thank God. Will I get it? My daughter's only twelve, does she need checking?",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): It puts your risk up a bit. We don't check a twelve year old. Arm up, I'm examining the left side.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (DOCTOR): Firm lump, upper outer left breast, roughly two centimetres. Skin not tethered. Nipple looks normal. Axilla is empty.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Is 2 centimetres big? Could it be a cyst? If the armpit is clear can it still be cancer? Will a biopsy hurt?",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (DOCTOR): Can't say from feeling it. Could be a cyst or a benign lump, and I can't rule out a cancer.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): What's booked. Nurse takes your bloods Thursday morning, fasting, nothing to eat or drink after midnight. Urgent breast clinic Thursday week at 1, they'll do the mammogram in that visit. I'll see you back here in two weeks.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (DOCTOR): If the mammogram comes back borderline, then we do an ultrasound. Not before. If the skin changes or the lump gets painful before the clinic, don't wait, come straight back."
 ],
